  </section>

  <p class="blurb">The Nasdaq 100 reshuffles once a year in December (ranked by end-of-November market cap); the rest of the year, special rebalances fire when a constituent falls below the minimum-weight threshold, gets acquired, or moves its listing. Sixty-plus changes since 2020 — the tech index&#39;s self-renewal in plain text.</p>

  <section class="answer">
    <h2>What this page answers</h2>
    <p class="conclusion">72 constituent rebalancings are officially documented. The latest revision took effect on 2026-10-09: MRNA added, WBD deleted. The evolutionary turnover of the Nasdaq 100 is continuous — passive index ownership fundamentally represents a systematically curated, self-cleansing basket of corporate leaders.</p><p>The Nasdaq 100 reshuffles once a year in December (ranked by end-of-November market cap); the rest of the year, special rebalances fire when a constituent falls below the minimum-weight threshold, gets acquired, or moves its listing. Sixty-plus changes since 2020 — the tech index&#39;s self-renewal in plain text. The data is refreshed by the History of Market pipeline and published as a stable JSON endpoint for research, citation, and AI-agent use.</p>
  </section>

